text:
Traccar checks whether the straight segment between two consecutive positions crosses a geofence, so that a fast vehicle that passed through a geofence between two reports still triggers the event. This works for polygon geofences, but a polyline geofence (a route, a line) never reports that a segment crosses it.

Make segment intersection work for polyline geofences: a segment crosses a polyline when it intersects any of its edges. A polyline is open: there is no edge between its last and its first point (unlike a polygon). Reuse the logic that polygons already use where you can, without changing how polygons behave.

Done when:
- a segment that crosses a polyline geofence is detected, and one that does not cross it (including one that would only cross the missing closing edge) is not;
- polygon geofences behave as before;
- the change is covered by tests;
- the existing test suite still passes.
